; When Ledger infers the price in a transaction with two commodities and no
; stated cost, the commodity of the first posting is the one bought, unless
; only the other is already a price target.  Here that is the hours, which
; take the cost as lots of 10h {$150} and 2h {€150}, so -V values them at
; those prices and --basis reports what was billed.
;
; The balance holds 10h reduced to 36000s, but the posting's commodity is
; looked for unreduced, as h, so neither component matches and the choice
; falls to the component that entered the balance first, the hours, on
; every run, as in 3.4.1.  Left to the order in which a balance keeps its
; components, which changes from run to run, some runs would buy the
; dollars instead, putting a lot of $-1500 {24s} on Income:Acme and
; leaving -V and --basis in hours.  $ sorts before s and € after it, so no
; fixed order of the two components can pass for the first posting's
; commodity in both transactions.

2024/01/05 Acme
    Assets:Billable              10h
    Income:Acme               $-1500

2024/01/20 Globex
    Assets:Billable               2h
    Income:Globex              €-300

test bal -V --now 2024/12/31
               $1500
                €300  Assets:Billable
              $-1500
               €-300  Income
              $-1500    Acme
               €-300    Globex
--------------------
                   0
end test

test reg --lots
24-Jan-05 Acme                  Assets:Billable        10.00h {$150} [2024/01/05] 10.00h {$150} [2024/01/05]
                                Income:Acme                  $-1500       $-1500
                                                      10.00h {$150} [2024/01/05]
24-Jan-20 Globex                Assets:Billable        2.00h {€150} [2024/01/20]       $-1500
                                                      10.00h {$150} [2024/01/05]
                                                       2.00h {€150} [2024/01/20]
                                Income:Globex                 €-300       $-1500
                                                      10.00h {$150} [2024/01/05]
                                                       2.00h {€150} [2024/01/20]
                                                                           €-300
end test

test bal --basis
               $1500
                €300  Assets:Billable
              $-1500
               €-300  Income
              $-1500    Acme
               €-300    Globex
--------------------
                   0
end test
